Hi,

A small bug in the install: after the install, there's no getty at the
serial console.  If you only have a serial console and didn't start
sshd, that's a wee bit annoying.

Regards, Maurice

From openbsd-alpha  Sat Dec 30 16:31:48 2006
From: Maurice Janssen <maurice () z74 ! net>
Date: Sat, 30 Dec 2006 16:31:48 +0000
To: openbsd-alpha
Subject: suggestion for INSTALL.alpha
Message-Id: <20061230163148.GC5337 () lyra ! z74 ! net>
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=116749777728803

Hi,

Recently I got a DEC 3000/300x machine.  At first, I couldn't get the
machine to boot over the network.  It appears that you need to add
	always-reply-rfc1048 on;
to the dhcpd.conf file.  Without this option, the DEC refuses to load
the netboot file with tftp.  With this option, it works like a charm.

It might help others if this is mentioned in the INSTALL.alpha file.

Regards,
Maurice

